# Gitignored local state that `scrape --git` worktrees still need.
# A fresh worktree only holds tracked files, so list anything gitignored that a scrape reads here.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repository root, `#` starts a comment.
# An optional last word picks how the path is brought over: `symlink` (the default), `hardlink` (files only) or `copy`.
# Every entry must exist and be gitignored, otherwise the scrape aborts with a configuration error.
#
# Example:
#   .env
#   some/local/cache copy
